The whole point of the scientific method, all the epistemology that I
know of, and much of the point of this list is to "Let your ideas Die
in your stead!"  

I find the stakes in Eric Raymond's challenge to Tim May to be
chicken-shit.

I consider Eric Raymond to be a fine contributor to the list.  I also
consider his pagan beliefs to be bogus.  I also like him personally.
If the challenge is about the ideas, then let the challenge be about
the ideas.

The stakes:  If Tim finds paganism to be bogus (not rational, etc.)
then Eric:
	1) quits talking about them on the list
	2) seriously considers that maybe Tim is right
	3) stays on the list to hear what non-pagans think
	4) read "Retreat to Commitment" by Bartley

Leaving the list if the ideas are judged as non-rational means that
the ideas are not the thing being challenged.  I know that some people
have already leaned on Tim to fudge the judgement so that Eric can
remain on the list.  I'm quite sure Tim won't do that (whichever way
he judges), and I also don't want Eric leaving (take your medicine
Eric :-)

Tim already outlined his stakes:  if he finds for paganism, he'll be
looking for a coven.  NOTE: he'll be taking the ideas to heart, not
denying that they are rational.  

If the ideas are being challenged, then they should be the ones to
leave the list if judged irrational, not Eric.  If Eric is doing the
challenging, then they should leave Eric, as well (his
responsibility).

Otherwise the challenge completely misses the point of what
rationality is!

